C Compilation Process and Errors
# C Compilation Process and Errors

## 📌 Overview

This repository contains my C programming notes and examples for understanding the complete C compilation process using GCC.

The C program passes through **four major stages**:

1. **Preprocessor**
2. **Compiler**
3. **Assembler**
4. **Linker**

It also covers **four major types of errors**:

1. **Preprocessor Error**
2. **Compile-Time Error**
3. **Linker Error**
4. **Run-Time Error**

---

# 🔄 Complete Compilation Process

```text
Source Code (.c)
       ↓
Preprocessor
       ↓
Preprocessed Code (.i)
       ↓
Compiler
       ↓
Assembly Code (.s)
       ↓
Assembler
       ↓
Object Code (.o)
       ↓
Linker
       ↓
Executable File
       ↓
Execution
STEP 1 — PREPROCESSOR
Description

The preprocessor is the first stage of the C compilation process.

It processes preprocessor directives before actual compilation.

Common Preprocessor Directives
#include
#define
#ifdef
#ifndef
#if
#else
#endif
Example
#include <stdio.h>

#define MESSAGE "Hello World"

int main()
{
    printf("%s\n", MESSAGE);

    return 0;
}
Command
gcc -E program.c -o program.i
Output File
program.i
Flow
program.c
   ↓
Preprocessor
   ↓
program.i
STEP 2 — COMPILER
Description

The compiler translates the preprocessed C source code into assembly code.

It also checks the program for C language and syntax errors.

Command
gcc -S program.i -o program.s
Output File
program.s
Flow
program.i
   ↓
Compiler
   ↓
program.s

The .s file contains assembly instructions.

STEP 3 — ASSEMBLER
Description

The assembler converts assembly language into object/machine code.

Command
gcc -c program.s -o program.o
Output File
program.o
Flow
program.s
   ↓
Assembler
   ↓
program.o

The object file contains machine code but may still contain unresolved references that need to be handled by the linker.

STEP 4 — LINKER
Description

The linker combines object files with required libraries.

It resolves external symbols and creates the final executable.

For example:

printf()

is provided by the C standard library.

Command
gcc program.o -o program
Output
program
Flow
program.o + Libraries
          ↓
        Linker
          ↓
      Executable
▶️ EXECUTION

After creating the executable:

./program
Example Output
Hello World
